From 35e5a2157fdb206caccc292fd912e7eb1cfc8782 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nuk3s <44327449+nuk3s@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:45:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kv-offload): evict a full tier from the tail of each
 chain

Upstream base: the patch applies to local-inference-lab/vllm at
19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 after the 702 patches of
spark-ds41f-1120 (candidate-62, 0001 to 0829) and patches 9030 to 9036
of this series.

Rationale: free_blocks evicts first the block that was freed first, and
stores free their blocks in prefix order over many events. A full tier
therefore evicted the start of each session first, and every block
behind that gap stayed resident although no lookup could reach it. A
session whose prefix hit in the GPU pool also never refreshed its copy
on disk, so the start of a busy session aged out first. With this patch,
when a finished request has no store left in flight (in eager mode), its
reachable chain in the offload pool is freed again in descending order
of block end position. The chain then sits at the recent end of the LRU
list, and its tail is evicted first. The reachable chain is the run of
the full-attention group up to its first missing block, together with
the cached blocks of the other prefix-cacheable groups that end inside
that run. A finished request now also waits for its finish-time store
before its state is cleaned up, and a degraded tier releases such a
request when it drops the queued store.

Quality implications: the patch does not change outputs. A full tier now
keeps a usable prefix of each recent session in place of blocks that no
lookup can reach.

Tests: tests/v1/simple_kv_offload/test_ds41_tier_eviction.py holds 8
tests on the real KVCacheManager and SimpleCPUOffloadScheduler with the
DS41 layout. They check the order of the chain after a finish, a full
tier that evicts a session from its tail with at most one checkpoint
stranded, two sessions that share a prefix, a session that grows over
three requests from hits in the GPU pool, the 18,724 slots of the 4 GiB
profile filled past twice their count, the wait for the finish-time
store, and the release by a degraded tier. On the tree of 9036, before
this patch, 6 of the 8 tests fail, while the layout and slot-count
tests pass on both trees. On the CPU path the offload suite passed 170
tests, with 2 CUDA-only modules skipped. On DGX Spark hardware the patch
ran only as part of the whole series.

Upstream status: the patch is proposed to spark-ds41f in
experiments/2026-11-22-kv-disk-tier and has not been submitted to
local-inference-lab/vllm.
